{"entity":{"id":"cs:339","name":"Albania","dataset":"cshapes","kind":"polity"},"territories":[{"id":10211,"name":"Albania","set_id":"cs","class":"dependency","valid_from":1913,"valid_to":1914.1780821917807,"snapshot_held":0,"area_km2":28656.5,"border_precision":3,"capital_name":"Vlore","sovereign":null,"sovereign_note":null,"modern_name":"Albania","min_lon":19.288536,"min_lat":39.645,"max_lon":21.053327,"max_lat":42.660345,"source_file":"CShapes-2.0.geojson","source_row":"gwcode=339;start=1913-1-1"},{"id":10212,"name":"Albania","set_id":"cs","class":"kingdom","valid_from":1914.1780821917807,"valid_to":1920.1120218579235,"snapshot_held":0,"area_km2":28656.5,"border_precision":3,"capital_name":"Durres","sovereign":null,"sovereign_note":null,"modern_name":"Albania","min_lon":19.288536,"min_lat":39.645,"max_lon":21.053327,"max_lat":42.660345,"source_file":"CShapes-2.0.geojson","source_row":"gwcode=339;start=1914-3-7"},{"id":10213,"name":"Albania","set_id":"cs","class":"republic","valid_from":1920.1120218579235,"valid_to":2020,"snapshot_held":0,"area_km2":28656.5,"border_precision":3,"capital_name":"Tirane","sovereign":null,"sovereign_note":null,"modern_name":"Albania","min_lon":19.288536,"min_lat":39.645,"max_lon":21.053327,"max_lat":42.660345,"source_file":"CShapes-2.0.geojson","source_row":"gwcode=339;start=1920-2-11"}],"identities":[{"qid":"Q582781","from_t":1913,"to_t":1914.1397260273973,"method":"name-template+date","confidence":0.9184779177467334,"label":"Independent Albania","description":"1912-1914 republic in Europe, first iteration of Albania as a sovereign state","inception":1912.9071038251366,"dissolved":1914.1397260273973,"enwiki":"Independent Albania","summary":"Independent Albania (Albanian: Shqipëria e Pavarur) was a parliamentary state declared in Vlorë (at the time part of Ottoman Empire) on 28 November 1912 during the First Balkan War. Its assembly was constituted on the same day while its government and senate were established on 5 December 1912.\nThe delegation of Albania submitted a memorandum to the London Conference of 1913 requesting international recognition of independent Albania. At the beginning of the conference it was decided that the region of Albania would be under Ottoman suzerainty but with an autonomous government."},{"qid":"Q187035","from_t":1914.1397260273973,"to_t":1925.0821917808219,"method":"name-template+date","confidence":0.9018372451364093,"label":"Principality of Albania","description":"1914-1925 monarchy in Europe, predecessor of modern Albania","inception":1914.1397260273973,"dissolved":1925.0821917808219,"enwiki":"Principality of Albania","summary":"The Principality of Albania (Albanian: Principata e Shqipërisë) was a monarchy from 1914 to 1925. It was headed by Wilhelm, Prince of Albania, and located in modern Albania in the Balkan region of Europe. The Ottoman Empire owned the land until the First Balkan War (1912—1913), which ended in the Treaty of London that formed the principality. The Principality of Albania survived invasions during World War I (1914–1918) and subsequent disputes over Albanian independence during the Paris Peace Conference (1919–1920)."},{"qid":"Q1923781","from_t":1925.0821917808219,"to_t":1928.6666666666667,"method":"name-template+date","confidence":0.909259261347319,"label":"Albanian Republic","description":"1925-1928 sovereign state in Europe, predecessor of modern Albania","inception":1925.0821917808219,"dissolved":1928.6666666666667,"enwiki":"Albanian Republic (1925–1928)","summary":"The Albanian Republic (Albanian: Republika Shqiptare) was the official name of Albania as enshrined in the Constitution of 1925. Albania came into an alliance with the Kingdom of Italy after signing the Treaties of Tirana, which gave Italy a monopoly on shipping and trade concessions. Albania was declared a constitutional monarchy in 1928. Upon its inception, Italy demanded to be allies with the republic."},{"qid":"Q1048340","from_t":1928.6666666666667,"to_t":1939.2630136986302,"method":"name-alias+date","confidence":0.8289335673912326,"label":"Albanian Kingdom","description":"period in 20th century Albanian history","inception":1928.6666666666667,"dissolved":1939.268493150685,"enwiki":"Albanian Kingdom (1928–1939)","summary":"The Albanian Kingdom (Gheg Albanian: Mbretnija Shqiptare; Tosk Albanian: Mbretëria Shqiptare) was the official name of Albania between 1928 and 1939. It was established when the Albanian parliament declared the country a monarchy, and President Ahmet Bej Zogu was proclaimed Zog I. This transition marked the end of the Albanian Republic and the beginning of a constitutional monarchy. Zog I's reign was characterized by efforts to modernize the country, including legal reforms and infrastructure development, although his government maintained his authoritarian practices as president.\nThe kingdom maintained close relations with Fascist Italy, which provided financial and military support."},{"qid":"Q1448131","from_t":1939.2630136986302,"to_t":1943.6849315068494,"method":"name-template+date","confidence":0.9122698195551103,"label":"Italian protectorate of Albania","description":"kingdom in Southeast Europe between 1939–1943","inception":1939.2630136986302,"dissolved":1943.6849315068494,"enwiki":"Kingdom of Albania in personal union with Italy","summary":"The Kingdom of Albania was in personal union with the  Kingdom of Italy (Fascist Italy) following the Italian invasion of Albania in 1939 and until the German occupation in September 1943.  It is also referred to as Italian Albania or Greater Albania, and was a state controlled by Fascist Italy. The monarch was Italian King, Victor Emmanuel III, who was represented in Albania by Italian governors. During this time, Albania ceased to exist as an independent country and became an autonomous part of the Italian Empire."},{"qid":"Q222","from_t":1943.6849315068494,"to_t":2020,"method":"name-label+date","confidence":0.95,"label":"Albania","description":"country in southeastern Europe","inception":1912.9071038251366,"dissolved":null,"enwiki":"Albania","summary":"Albania, officially the Republic of Albania, is a country in Southeastern Europe. It is located in the Balkans, on the Adriatic and Ionian Seas within the Mediterranean Sea, and shares land borders with Montenegro to the northwest, Kosovo to the northeast, North Macedonia to the east and Greece to the south. With an area of 28,748 km2 (11,100 sq mi), it has a varied range of climatic, geological, hydrological and morphological conditions. Landscapes range from rugged snow-capped mountains in the Albanian Alps and the Korab, Skanderbeg, Pindus and Ceraunian Mountains, to fertile lowland plains extending from the Adriatic and Ionian sea coasts."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q582781","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q159610","value_label":"Vlorë","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Vlorë"},{"qid":"Q582781","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q166747","value_label":"parliamentary system","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"parliamentary system"},{"qid":"Q582781","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q187035","value_label":"Principality of Albania","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Principality of Albania"},{"qid":"Q582781","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q730163","value_label":"Autonomous Republic of Northern Epirus","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Autonomous Republic of Northern Epirus"},{"qid":"Q582781","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flag of Albanian Provisional Government (1912-1914).svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q187035","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q83285","value_label":"Durrës","from_t":1914.1780821917807,"to_t":1920,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Durrës"},{"qid":"Q1