,"property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Skënder Gjinushi"},{"qid":"Q222","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q733779","value_label":"Pjetër Arbnori","from_t":1992.2622950819673,"to_t":1992.2704918032787,"title":"President of Albania","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Pjetër Arbnori"},{"qid":"Q222","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q1722312","value_label":"Kastriot Islami","from_t":1992.2540983606557,"to_t":1992.2622950819673,"title":"President of Albania","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Kastriot Islami"},{"qid":"Q222","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q150642","value_label":"Victor Emmanuel III of Italy","from_t":1939.2876712328766,"to_t":1943.6849315068494,"title":"King of Albania","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Victor Emmanuel III of Italy"},{"qid":"Q222","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q57594","value_label":"William, Prince of Albania","from_t":1914,"to_t":1925,"title":"King of Albania","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"William, Prince of Albania"},{"qid":"Q222","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q60699","value_label":"Zog I of Albania","from_t":1928.6666666666667,"to_t":1939.2630136986302,"title":"King of Albania","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Zog I of Albania"},{"qid":"Q222","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q48409","value_label":"Flag of Albania.svg","from_t":1992.2650273224044,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Albania","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Albania"}],"people":{"Q107422711":{"label":"Bajram Begaj","description":"president of Albania","enwiki":"Bajram Begaj","summary":"Bajram Begaj (born 20 March 1967) is an Albanian politician and military officer serving as president of Albania since 2022. Prior to his election as president, he served as the 26th Chief of General Staff of the Albanian Armed Forces from July 2020 to June 2022. On 3 June 2022, Begaj was officially nominated by the governing Socialist Party as the candidate for the fourth round of the 2022 presidential election. He is the second president in post-communist Albania to come from a predominantly military background.","image":"Prime Minister Keir Starmer meets Albania President Bajram Begaj (54521430145) (cropped).jpg","birth":1967.213698630137,"death":null},"Q316901":{"label":"Edi Rama","description":"Prime Minister of Albania since 2013 (born 1964)","enwiki":"Edi Rama","summary":"Edvin Kristaq \"Edi\" Rama (born 4 July 1964) is an Albanian politician, artist, writer, and former professional basketball player who has served as prime minister of Albania since 2013 and as chairman of the Socialist Party of Albania since 2005. He was the Minister of Culture, Youth and Sports from 1998 to 2000 and the Mayor of Tirana from 2000 to 2011.\nA coalition of centre-left parties led by Rama in the 2013 parliamentary election defeated the incumbent centre-right coalition led by Sali Berisha of the Democratic Party of Albania. Rama was appointed prime minister for additional terms following parliamentary elections in 2017, 2021, and 2025.","image":"Edi Rama (2024-02-29).jpg","birth":1964.5054644808743,"death":null},"Q156833":{"label":"Ramiz Alia","description":"former First Secretary of the Party of Labour of Albania, 1st President of the Republic of Albania (1925-2011)","enwiki":"Ramiz Alia","summary":"Ramiz Alia (18 October 1925 – 7 October 2011) was an Albanian politician serving as the second and last leader of the People's Socialist Republic of Albania from 1985 to 1991, serving as First Secretary of the Party of Labour of Albania. He was also the country's head of state from 1982 to 1992. He had been seen as a successor by Enver Hoxha and took power after Hoxha died.","image":"Ramiz Alia (portret).jpg","birth":1925.7945205479452,"death":2011.7643835616439},"Q190889":{"label":"Alfred Moisiu","description":"Albanian general and politician; former President of Albania (born 1929)","enwiki":"Alfred Moisiu","summary":"Alfred Spiro Moisiu (born 1 December 1929) is an  Albanian military general, diplomat and politician who served as the president of Albania from 2002 to 2007. He is the oldest son of Albanian Army general Spiro Moisiu.","image":"AlfredMoisiu.png","birth":1929.9150684931508,"death":null},"Q212666":{"label":"Haxhi Lleshi","description":"Albanian politician (1913-1998)","enwiki":"Haxhi Lleshi","summary":"Haxhi Lleshi (1 May 1913 – 1 January 1998) was an Albanian military leader and communist politician who served as the Chairman of the Presidium of the People's Assembly of the People's Socialist Republic of Albania from 1953 to 1982.","image":"Haxhi Lleshi 1943.jpg","birth":1913.7972602739726,"death":1998},"Q294250":{"label":"Rexhep Meidani","description":"Albanian politician","enwiki":"Rexhep Meidani","summary":"Rexhep Qemal Meidani (; born 17 August 1944) is an Albanian physicist, professor, diplomat and politician. Meidani was the president of Albania from 1997 to 2002, and the second to be elected after the first multi-party elections in 1991.","image":"Rexhep Meidani.jpg","birth":1944.6256830601094,"death":null},"Q560630":{"label":"Omer Nishani","description":"Albanian politician (1887-1954)","enwiki":"Omer Nishani","summary":"Omer Nishani (5 February 1887 – 26 May 1954) was an Albanian medical doctor and political figure involved first in the struggle against Ahmet Zogu (known after 1928 as King Zog) in the 1920s and 1930s, and then in the struggle against the fascist occupation of Albania during the 1942–44 period, becoming Chairman of the Presidium of the People's Assembly of the People's Republic of Albania (thereby becoming the country's head of state) in 1946 and serving in this position until 1953.","image":"Omer Nishani.jpg","birth":1887.0958904109589,"death":1954.3972602739725},"Q57300":{"label":"Bamir Topi","description":"Albanian diplomat and politician","enwiki":"Bamir Topi","summary":"Bamir Myrteza Topi (born 24 April 1957) is an Albanian diplomat and politician who served as President of Albania from 2007 to 2012.\nTopi was the honorary president of the Albanian football club KF Tirana from 2005 to 2007. In September 2012, Topi became the leader of the New Democratic Spirit party.","image":"Bamir Topi 2.jpg","birth":1957.309589041096,"death":null},"Q57526":{"label":"Bujar Nishani","description":"Albanian politician (1966–2022)","enwiki":"Bujar Nishani","summary":"Bujar Faik Nishani (Albanian pronunciation: [bujaɾ ni'ʃani]; 29 September 1966 – 28 May 2022) was an Albanian politician who served as President of Albania from 2012 to 2017.\nNishani was the youngest person to have been chosen as president of Albania, taking office at the age of 47. Before his election as president, Nishani held a number of governmental and diplomatic positions. Namely, he served as Minister of Internal Affairs from 2007 to 2009, and again between 2011 and 2012, as well as Minister of Justice from 2009 to 2011.","image":"Bujar Nishani (03-10-2016).jpg","birth":1966.7424657534248,"death":2022.4027397260274},"Q57625":{"label":"Sali Berisha","description":"Albanian politician","enwiki":"Sali Berisha","summary":"Sali Berisha (Albanian: [saˈli bɛˈɾiʃa] ; born 15 October 1944) is an Albanian politician and retired cardiologist who served as the President of Albania from 1992 to 1997 and as the 32nd prime minister of Albania from 2005 to 2013. Berisha has served as chairman of the Democratic Party of Albania since 2022. He has previously held the position of chairman from 1990 to 1992 and 1997 to 2013. He is the leader of the opposition in Albania.","image":"Sali Berisha 2025.jpg","birth":1944.7868852459017,"death":null},"Q60699":{"label":"Zog I of Albania","description":"Albanian prime minister, president and king (1895-1961) (r.1922-1939)","enwiki":"Zog I","summary":"Zog I (born Ahmed Muhtar Bey Zogolli; 8 October 1895 – 9 April 1961) was an Albanian statesman and aristocrat who served as the leader of Albania from 1922 to 1939. At age 27, he first served as Albania's youngest ever prime minister (1922–1924), then as president (1925–1928), and finally as king (1928–1939).\nBorn to an aristocratic beylical family in Ottoman Albania, Zogolli was active in Albanian politics from a young age and fought for Austria-Hungary in World War I. In 1922, he adopted the surname Zogu. He held various ministerial posts in the Albanian government before being driven into exile in June 1924, but returned later that year with Yugoslav and White Russian military support and was elected prime minister.","image":"King Zog I.jpg","birth":1895.7671232876712,"death":1961.268493150685},"Q727132":{"label":"Ilir Meta","description":"President of Albania from 2017 to 2022","enwiki":"Ilir Meta","summary":"Ilir Rexhep Meta (Albanian pronunciation: [iliɾ meta]; born 24 March 1969) is an Albanian politician who served as President of Albania from 2017 to 2022.\nPreviously Meta served as Prime Minister from 1999 to 2002 and he was Speaker of the Parliament of Albania from 2013 to 2017. He also held positions as Deputy Prime Minister, Minister for Europe and Foreign Affairs and Minister of Economy, Trade, and Energy. Prior to that, he held the Chairmanship of the Parliamentary Commission of European Integration.","image":"President of Albania Ilir Meta.jpg","birth":1969.2246575342465,"death":null},"Q3108905":{"label":"Skënder Gjinushi","description":"Albanian mathematician and politician (born 1949)","enwiki":"Skënder Gjinushi","summary":"Skënder Gjinushi (born 24 December 1949 in Vlorë, Albania) is an Albanian politician and academic. He has served in several high-ranking positions in the Albanian government, including as Speaker of Parliament and Deputy Prime Minister. He founded the Social Democratic Party of Albania and served as its chairman from 1991 to 2019. He is currently serving as the president of the Academy of Sciences of Albania.","image":null,"birth":1949.978082191781,"death":null},"Q733779":{"label":"Pjetër Arbnori","description":"Albanian politician (1935-2006)","enwiki":"Pjetër Arbnori","summary":"Pjetër Filip Arbnori (18 January 1935 – 8 July 2006) was an Albanian politician and dissident of the communist regime in Albania. He was dubbed \"the Mandela of the Balkans\" by Albanian statesmen because of the length of his 28-year internment. He was born in Durrës, on the Adriatic coast. President Topi bestowed the Nation's Honor Order upon Pjetër Arbnori (post mortem).","image":"Stamp of Albania - 2007 - Colnect 374807 - Pjetër Arbnori 1935-2006 former acting Albanian President.jpeg","birth":1935.0465753424658,"death":2006.5150684931507},"Q1722312":{"label":"Kastriot Islami","description":"Albanian politician","enwiki":"Kastriot Islami","summary":"Kastriot Muhamet Islami (born 18 August 1952) is an Albanian politician. Formerly a member of the Communist Party of Albania, turned moderate Socialist. He was Chairman of the Parliament of Albania from April 17, 1991 to April 6, 1992. On April 3, 1992, when the last communist president, Ramiz Alia resigned, Islami served as acting president for three days.","image":"Kastriot Islami 2004.jpg","birth":1952.6284153005465,"death":null},"Q150642":{"label":"Victor Emmanuel III of Italy","description":"King of Italy from 1900 to 1946","enwiki":"Victor Emmanuel III","summary":"Victor Emmanuel III (Italian: Vittorio Emanuele Ferdinando Maria Gennaro di Savoia; 11 November 1869 – 28 December 1947) was King of Italy from 29 July 1900 until his abdication on 9 May 1946. A member of the House of Savoy, he also reigned as Emperor of Ethiopia from 1936 to 1941 and King of the Albanians from 1939 to 1943, following the Italian invasions of Ethiopia and Albania. During his reign of nearly 46 years, which began after the assassination of his father Umberto I, the Kingdom of Italy became involved in World War I and in World War II. His reign also encompassed the birth, rise, and fall of the Fascist regime.\nThe first fourteen years of Victor Emmanuel's reign were dominated by prime minister Giovanni Giolitti, who focused on industrialization and passed several democratic reforms, such as the introduction of universal male suffrage.","image":"Vitorio Emanuel III.jpg","birth":1869.8602739726027,"death":1947.9890410958903},"Q57594":{"label":"William, Prince of Albania","description":"Prince of Albania (1876–1945)","enwiki":"Wilhelm, Prince of Albania","summary":"Wilhelm, Prince of Albania (Wilhelm Friedrich Heinrich; Albanian: Vilhelm, Princ i Shqipërisë, 26 March 1876 – 18 April 1945) was sovereign of the Principality of Albania from 7 March to 3 September 1914. His reign officially came to an end on 31 January 1925, when the country was declared an Albanian Republic.\nOutside the country and in diplomatic correspondence, he was styled \"sovereign prince\", but in Albania, he was referred to as mbret, or king.","image":"Wilhelm zu Wied 1912 a.jpg","birth":1876.2322404371585,"death":1945.2931506849316}},"media":{"Flag of Albanian Provisional Government (1912-1914).svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Flag_of_Albanian_Provisional_Government_%281912-1914%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Albanian_Provisional_Government_%281912-1914%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Albanian_Provisional_Government_(1912-1914).svg","author":"Jaume Ollé (original); Ryan Wilson (derivative)","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"Flag of the Principality of Albania (1915).svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Flag_of_the_Principality_of_Albania_%281915%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Principality_of_Albania_%281915%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Principality_of_Albania_(1915).svg","author":"Vectorized by Kj1595","license":"Public domain"},"Great Arms of Prince Wilhelm of Wied.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Great_Arms_of_Prince_Wilhelm_of_Wied.svg/330px-Great_Arms_of_Prince_Wilhelm_of_Wied.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Arms_of_Prince_Wilhelm_of_Wied.svg","author":"Emil Doepler","license":"Public domain"},"Flag of Albania (1926–1928).svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Flag_of_Albania_%281926%E2%80%931928%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Albania_%281926%E2%80%931928%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Albania_(1926%E2%80%931928).svg","author":"Orange Tuesday (talk)","license":"Public domain"},"Variation of the Arms of State of the Albanian Republic (1926–1928).svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Variation_of_the_Arms_of_State_of_the_Albanian_Republic_%281926%E2%80%931928%29.svg/330px-Variation_of_the_Arms_of_State_of_the_Albanian_Republic_%281926%E2%80%931928%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Variation_of_the_Arms_of_State_of_the_Albanian_Republic_(1926%E2%80%931928).svg","author":"Samhanin","license":"Public domain"},"Flag of Albania (1934–1939).svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Flag_of_Albania_%281934%E2%80%931939%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Albania_%281934%E2%80%931939%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Albania_(1934%E2%80%931939).svg","author":"Original: Zscout370,  Fabiodevivo Vector:  LSDSL","license":"Public domain"},"CoA of the Kingdom of Albania (1928–1939).svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/CoA_of_the_Kingdom_of_Albania_%281928%E2%80%931939%29.svg/330px-CoA_of_the_Kingdom_of_Albania_%281928%E2%80%931939%29.svg.png?utm_source